<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Rotor Array Simulation</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="bundle.css">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="favicon.svg">
</head>
<body>
    <div id="app">
        <div id="canvas-container">
            <div id="canvas-stack">
                <canvas id="sim-canvas" class="sim-layer"></canvas>
                <canvas id="overlay-canvas" class="sim-layer"></canvas>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div id="sidebar">
            <h1>Rotor Array <button id="help-btn" title="Help">?</button></h1>
            
            <div id="controls-container">
                <!-- Controls will be injected here -->
            </div>

            <div class="control-group">
                <label>Mean Direction</label>
                <canvas id="mean-dir-canvas" class="mean-dir-canvas" width="240" height="240"></canvas>
            </div>

            <div class="control-group" id="color-bar-container">
            </div>

            <div class="control-group">
                <div class="value-display value-display-compact">
                    <span class="value-label">Energy (per rotor):</span>
                    <span id="energy-per-node-value">—</span>
                    <span class="value-sep"> | </span>
                    <span>dE/E0:</span>
                    <span id="energy-rel-dev-value">—</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="control-group">
                <label>Order Parameter (r)</label>
                <div id="uplot-chart"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="sidebar-footer">
                <p>&copy; {{YEAR}} {{OWNER}}</p>
                <p>Build: {{DATE}} ({{HASH}})</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <script type="module" src="main.js"></script>

    <div id="help-overlay">
        <div id="help-modal">
            <button id="close-help">&times;</button>
            <div id="help-content">
                <h2>Rotor Array Simulation - Help</h2>
                <p>This application simulates an L &times; L square array of coupled planar rotors subjected to a uniform external field, with periodic boundary conditions in both directions.</p>
                
                <h3>Physics Overview</h3>
                <div style="text-align: center; margin: 15px 0;">
                    {{LAGRANGIAN}}
                </div>
                <p>The system consists of N = L&sup2; rotors on a square lattice. Each rotor interacts with its four nearest neighbors via a coupling constant J and responds to an external field M.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Coupling (J)</strong>: Determines how strongly rotors want to align with their neighbors.</li>
                    <li><strong>Field (M)</strong>: Determines how strongly rotors want to align with the vertical downward direction (&theta; = 0).</li>
                    <li><strong>Order Parameter (r)</strong>: Measures the synchronization of the system. A value of 1.0 means all rotors are perfectly aligned.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Controls</h3>
                <p><strong>Simulation Parameters</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Lattice Side (L)</strong>: Adjust the dimension of the square lattice. Changeable only when paused.</li>
                    <li><strong>Initial Condition Preset</strong>: Choose a starting configuration:
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Random Angles</strong>: High entropy start.</li>
                            <li><strong>Twisted</strong>: Topological winding state. Use <strong>Winding (k)</strong> to set full rotations.</li>
                            <li><strong>Domain Wall</strong>: Split configuration (left/right).</li>
                            <li><strong>Pi/2 Domain Wall</strong>: Split configuration with &plusmn;&pi;/2 regions.</li>
                            <li><strong>Vortex Band</strong>: Phase wraps across a band; use <strong>Wraps (k)</strong>, <strong>Width (w)</strong>, and <strong>Shift (&delta;&phi;)</strong>.</li>
                            <li><strong>Cross Domain</strong>: Quadrant-style phase domains.</li>
                            <li><strong>Vortex Pair</strong>: Opposite topological charges.</li>
                            <li><strong>Skyrmion</strong>: Localized phase twist.</li>
                            <li><strong>Single Kick</strong>: Gaussian velocity kick at the center.</li>
                            <li><strong>Thermalized</strong>: Random velocities assigned to rotors.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li><strong>Coupling (J)</strong> &amp; <strong>Field (M)</strong>: Real-time sliders for interaction and field strength.</li>
                    <li><strong>Time Scale</strong>: Simulation speed multiplier.</li>
                    <li><strong>Initial Temp (T)</strong>: Adds thermal noise to initial velocities.</li>
                    <li><strong>Show Arrows</strong>: Toggle rotor direction arrows when zoomed in.</li>
                </ul>
                
                <p><strong>Controls &amp; Monitors</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Start/Stop</strong>: Runs or pauses the integration.</li>
                    <li><strong>Apply</strong>: Applies current settings and restarts the simulation.</li>
                    <li><strong>Order Parameter Plot</strong>: Shows the history of system synchronization.</li>
                    <li><strong>Mean Direction</strong>: Shows the current average rotor direction.</li>
                    <li><strong>Energy (per rotor)</strong> and <strong>dE/E0</strong>: Track energy and relative drift.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Visualization</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Hue</strong>: Represents the rotor's angular variable &theta; &in; [0, 2&pi;). &theta; = 0 corresponds to pointing straight down.</li>
                    <li><strong>Luminosity</strong>: Brighter colors indicate higher kinetic energy (&omega;&sup2;). Zero energy is dim but visible.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
